  "steps": [
    "<strong>Red Curry Paste:</strong> Deseed chillies and soak in warm water 15 min; reserve 1–2 tbsp soaking water. Blitz onion first into a loose paste. Add chillies and remaining paste ingredients; blend smooth, adding reserved water as needed.",
    "<strong>Prepare Tofu:</strong> Wrap tofu in kitchen towels, weigh down lightly, and drain 10–15 min. Pat dry, slice, and coat lightly with corn flour.",
    "Heat 1–2 tbsp oil in a pan over medium. Pan-fry tofu until golden on both sides. Remove and set aside.",
    "In the same pan, add remaining oil, onion, garlic, ginger, curry paste, and hot sauce. Cook 2–3 min until fragrant.",
    "Stir in coconut milk, brown sugar, soy sauce, and lemon juice. Simmer a few minutes until slightly thickened.",
    "Return tofu to the pan and gently coat in the sauce. Garnish with scallions and sesame seeds. Serve hot with rice."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Use firm tofu if you want extra crisp edges.",
    "Add kaffir lime zest or lime juice at the end for extra brightness.",
    "Great with jasmine rice or coconut rice."
  ]
